Every piece of modern technology relies on one thing: the network. Whether it’s streaming Sunday’s service, running a business point-of-sale system, or managing security cameras, your network is the backbone that makes it all work.

That’s why at Brink Design, we recommend and install **UniFi networks**. From routers and switches to Wi-Fi and cameras, UniFi delivers reliable, scalable solutions that keep your technology connected—day in and day out. For businesses and churches in Rapid City and across South Dakota, it’s the foundation of a system that “just works.”

---

## Why UniFi for Business and Church Networks?

Unlike consumer-grade gear or patchwork installs, UniFi offers a professional, all-in-one platform designed for performance and reliability.

**Benefits of UniFi networks include:**

- **Seamless Wi-Fi Coverage:** Multiple access points provide strong signals in every room.
- **Powerful Routers & Switches:** Handle dozens (or hundreds) of devices without slowdowns.
- **Unified Management:** Monitor your entire network from a single dashboard.
- **Built-in Security:** Advanced firewall and threat detection to protect your data.
- **Integration with AV:** Cameras, door access, and AV systems run smoothly on the same backbone.

🎯 **The result:** no more dropped livestreams, slow internet, or dead zones—just a network you can count on.

---

## Core Components of a UniFi Network

### 1. Routers (UniFi Dream Machine Pro / Pro Max)

The “brain” of your network—handling internet traffic, firewall security, and system management.

### 2. Switches (UniFi Pro & Enterprise Series)

Provide power (PoE) and connectivity for everything from Wi-Fi access points to IP phones and cameras.

### 3. Wi-Fi Access Points (UniFi U7 / U6 Series)

Deliver reliable, high-speed wireless coverage throughout your building with seamless roaming.

### 4. Cameras & Protect NVR

Surveillance built into the same network ecosystem—no messy third-party software required.

📷 *Pro Tip:* Because UniFi devices are all managed in the same interface, you get a true “single pane of glass” to monitor internet, Wi-Fi, and cameras at once.

---

## Case Study: Black River Contracting

When **Black River Contracting** built their new facility, they needed a robust network to support day-to-day operations, security, and future growth.

**The challenge:**

- Provide strong Wi-Fi coverage throughout offices and shop space
- Install a modern surveillance system
- Centralize management for easy operation

**Our UniFi solution:**

- UniFi Dream Machine Pro for routing and network management
- UniFi Pro 24 PoE switch powering all cameras and access points
- 7 × UniFi U7 Lite access points for whole-building Wi-Fi
- 9 × UniFi cameras for complete interior and exterior coverage
- Access control with UniFi Reader Flex and Door Hub

**The result:** a single, unified platform managing internet, Wi-Fi, security, and access control—all with scalability built in for the future.

